# Pointer capture (3-E1). The thumb is x 0..100, y 0..40 and captures on
# pointerdown; the track is y 40..80 and does not.
#
# Touch on the thumb is left out until 3-E4: Chromium cancels it at the
# first pan, as touch-action is auto, while vapors' RELAXED rule lets a
# capturing listener own the touch (touch-action: none, which vapors
# does not have yet).
listen pointerdown pointermove pointerup pointercancel gotpointercapture lostpointercapture click
capture div#thumb
move 50 20                    over the thumb
expect event pointermove div#thumb
press 50 20                   the thumb captures
expect event pointerdown div#thumb
move 50 60                    over the track, captured
expect event gotpointercapture div#thumb
expect event pointermove div#thumb
move 300 300                  off both, captured
expect event pointermove div#thumb
release 300 300               the capture ends; the click is the thumb's
expect event pointerup div#thumb
expect event lostpointercapture div#thumb
expect event click div#thumb
move 50 60                    the track again, not captured
expect event pointermove div#track
touch-down 50 60              a finger on the track
expect event pointerdown div#track
touch-move 50 20              40 px, past the 20 px tap slop: captured without asking, then the pan takes it
expect event gotpointercapture div#track
expect event pointercancel div#track
expect event lostpointercapture div#track
touch-up 50 20                cancelled: no pointerup
expect no event pointerup
